A cross-site iframe that used Web Locks got its web process killed.

When the iframe went away, the web process sent
WebLockRegistryProxy::ClientIsGoingAway, and the UI process checked the
iframe's ClientOrigin with WebProcessProxy::hasCommittedClientOrigin().  In a
process that also runs a service or shared worker, that function never looked
at the recorded commits: it only compared both origins with the process's
site, the main frame's.  An iframe from another site failed that comparison,
the message was treated as invalid, and the process was terminated -- luakit
shows "Web process crashed", and nothing is printed (the invalid-message log
is release logging, which this build does not have).  flaschenpost.de with
its Cloudflare Turnstile iframe did this every time.

The recorded commits are now checked first; the site comparison only covers
what they do not.  Same change as WebKit 314641@main (bug 314863).

